content:
{
  "asset": "P-104 standby pump, AquaDyne HF-300 on the filtered-water line; serial plate painted over and unreadable.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "The steady shaft-seal leak is a documented defect requiring mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No numerical allowable leakage rate or permissible operating time with this leak is supplied, so the leak cannot be classified against a quantitative limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reported vibration is 3.0 mm/s. On the HF-300 bearing-housing vibration chart, which is expressed in mm/s RMS, this is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary and below the 4.5 mm/s Zone B/C boundary. It is therefore provisionally Zone B, 'Long-term operation', not Zone C or the highest-severity Zone D. The reading is not on a boundary, so the figure's boundary ambiguity does not affect this classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reported housing temperature is 69 C. The applicable HF-300 bearing-housing surface limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. Thus 69 C is within the normal range, 11 C below alarm and 21 C below trip; the high-bearing-temperature troubleshooting branch is not triggered by this reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No immediate-stop or automatic priority-1 trigger is demonstrated by the supplied readings: 3.0 mm/s is below Zone D, and 69 C is below the 80 C alarm. Zone D requires an immediate stop and reliability-engineer notification before restart; a bearing temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit requires a priority-1 work order within the shift. P2 is therefore assigned for planned corrective seal work, but this does not establish that continued operation with the steady leak is acceptable.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces are a direct documented cause of shaft-seal leakage and should be checked first when the seal is removed. The report alone does not establish this cause or rank it conclusively above the other documented causes.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have run dry. The HF-300 uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry; flush availability and any dry-running history must be checked.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is another documented cause of seal leakage. Confirm it by laser alignment rather than inferring it from the present readings, because 3.0 mm/s is in Zone B and 69 C is normal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional fleet cause: if P-104 is serial HF3-22000 or above and contains the superseded HF3-450 component seal, the bulletin attributes early failures to a revised sleeve tolerance. The unreadable serial and unknown installed seal prevent this cause from being confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Serial-identification hold point: before seal selection, seal-parts issue or gland reassembly, obtain a verified pump serial from site records or other reliable identification. If it cannot be established, hold the seal replacement for engineering disposition; do not default to either bulletin branch.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Isolate and drain the pump for seal work. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain the line-break permit, draining and venting before line break.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. Remove the back pull-out assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, so use certified lifting equipment under a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "4. Remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and shaft sleeve, and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Inspect the removed seal for worn or cracked faces and investigate any evidence of dry running; retain the findings to establish the failure cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "5. If the verified serial is HF3-22000 or above, do not fit HF3-450. Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, which is pre-set and needs no sleeve measurement for seal setting. Tighten its seal gland nuts to 30 Nm. Separately inspect sleeve scoring and replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "6. If the verified serial is below HF3-22000, retain the manual branch: fit component mechanical seal HF3-450 and use Table 5, including M10 seal gland nuts at 25 Nm on lightly oiled threads. Do not apply the bulletin's 0.1 mm sleeve-replacement criterion to this branch as though it were a documented manual limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "7. Fit the selected new seal and a new HF3-120 casing gasket, then reassemble. For the other applicable Table 5 fasteners, with lightly oiled threads, tighten M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. Use the serial-specific gland torque from step 5 or 6; do not use 25 Nm on HF3-450B.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "8. Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool, as required by the seal-leak troubleshooting action and after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Accept only parallel offset of 0.05 mm and angular alignment of 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "9. Before operational testing, verify the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the seal dry. After repair, record vibration in mm/s RMS on the bearing housing and housing-surface temperature for comparison with the same limits. If vibration enters Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, quantity one only if P-104 is verified as serial HF3-22000 or above. It is pre-set and is mutually exclusive with HF3-450; do not issue or fit while the serial remains unresolved.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Component mechanical seal, quantity one only if P-104 is verified below serial HF3-22000. It is prohibited on pumps at or above that serial and is mutually exclusive with HF3-450B.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit one new gasket during the seal-replacement procedure and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional rather than routine replacement. For verified serial HF3-22000 or above, replace if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Any other replacement requires an inspection disposition because the supplied manual gives no numerical scoring limit for lower serials.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For this work on the pump seal, electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of both suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit are mandatory; drain and vent before line break.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the 25 kg lifting-control threshold. Provide a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm before starting whether the line has any chemical dosing. If the chemically-dosed-line condition applies, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the Plan 11 flush arrangement from pump discharge and never run the pump seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-alignment standard allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection: the manual parts list identifies HF3-450, while Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires HF3-450B only on HF-300 pumps at serial HF3-22000 and above. Pumps below that serial explicitly continue with HF3-450 and the manual. The serial-range rule, rather than blanket use of either document, governs this asset; because P-104's serial is unreadable, the decision remains on hold.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas the bulletin gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Use 30 Nm only on the verified HF3-22000-and-above/HF3-450B branch; use the manual's 25 Nm on the verified lower-serial/HF3-450 branch. No torque can be finally selected until the serial is known.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve-scoring coverage differs: the manual requires inspection but supplies no numerical rejection threshold, while the bulletin requires HF3-455 replacement when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth on pumps covered by its serial range. That threshold must not be extended to lower-serial or unidentified pumps without further evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is P-104's verified serial, and which seal is currently installed? The serial is necessary to choose between HF3-450/HF3-450B, 25/30 Nm and the applicable sleeve rule; if it cannot be recovered, an authorised engineering disposition is needed. (C13)",
    "Was the reported 3.0 mm/s vibration measured as RMS on the bearing housing, as required by Figure 3? If not, the provisional Zone B classification must be reviewed. (C07)",
    "Was 69 C measured on the bearing-housing surface, which is the manual's specified temperature measurement location? (C01, C02)",
    "Has the pump experienced dry running or interruption of its Plan 11 discharge flush, and are there prior alignment or seal-failure records that would distinguish the documented causes? (C02, C09)",
    "If the pump is below serial HF3-22000 and sleeve scoring is found, what acceptance or replacement limit applies? The supplied manual requires inspection but gives no numerical scoring threshold, and the bulletin's 0.1 mm criterion is serial-limited. (C10, C13)",
    "Can operations confirm that the filtered-water line is not chemically dosed and has no residual chemical exposure? If it is chemically dosed, add chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. (C15)",
    "What quantitative post-repair seal-leakage acceptance criterion and permissible operating response to the present steady leak should be used? The troubleshooting table prescribes replacement but supplies no leakage-rate or continued-operation limit. (C09)",
    "Confirm the site-required completion date and P2 classification: the evidence defines a priority-1 response for bearing temperature above the alarm limit but does not provide the site's P2/P3 priority definitions. The current 69 C reading does not activate that P1 rule. (C02, C15)"
  ]
}
